     "content": "### The Verdict: **Yes, accept the offer.**\n\nThis is an **exceptional outcome**. Getting a **$200,000 cash sign-on bonus** at Google L6 is rare (typically requiring VP/Comp Committee approval) [1]. They fully matched your Meta base, neutralized your unvested equity risk with guaranteed upfront cash, and kept the generous $1.08M stock grant [2].\n\nYou have extracted maximum value from this negotiation. Pushing further would yield diminishing returns and risk damaging goodwill before starting.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Numbers Breakdown\n\nWith Google\u2019s standard front-loaded vesting schedule (typically 33% / 33% / 22% / 12% or 38% / 32% / 20% / 10%), your cash flow over the next few years will significantly outpace Meta [2]:\n\n| Year | Base Salary | Target Bonus (20%) | Equity Vest (at ~33%/33%/22%/12%) | Sign-On Bonus | **Total Comp (Google)** | Current Meta Comp |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Year 1** | $240,000 | $48,000 | ~$356,400 | **$200,000** | **~$844,400** | ~$526,000 |\n| **Year 2** | $240,000 | $48,000 | ~$356,400 | $0 | **~$644,400** | ~$526,000 |\n| **Year 3** | $240,000 | $48,000 | ~$237,600 | $0 | **~$525,600** *(+ Refreshes)* | ~$526,000 |\n| **Year 4** | $240,000 | $48,000 | ~$129,600 | $0 | **~$417,600** *(+ Refreshes)* | ~$526,000 |\n\n#### Total 4-Year Guaranteed Value:\n* **Google:** **~$2.43 Million** *(average of ~$608,000/yr before any stock appreciation or annual refreshers)*\n* **Meta (Status Quo):** **~$2.10 Million** ($526k \u00d7 4)\n* **Net Financial Gain:** **+$330,000+**, with **$318,000+ of that excess realized in Year 1 alone**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why This Is a Clear \"Accept\"\n\n1. **Risk-Free Year 1 Transition:** The $200k sign-on completely covers the $200k in Meta RSUs you would forfeit over the next 12 months, but delivers it as **liquid cash** upfront rather than waiting for quarterly stock vests.\n2. **Top-of-Band Package:** A $2.43M 4-year baseline for an L6 PM is in the top 5\u201310% of Google compensation for this level [1, 2].\n3. **Resume / Pedigree Value:** Holding Senior PM (L6 / IC6) titles at both Meta and Google gives you elite Silicon Valley pedigree, unlocking Director / Principal / VP tracks across the tech ecosystem in the future.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Final Checklist Before Signing\n\nBefore returning the signed offer, double-check these administrative details with the recruiter:\n\n* **Sign-On Payout Schedule & Clawback:** Confirm if the $200k is paid on your first paycheck (standard) and verify the clawback clause (standard is a 1-year prorated clawback if you leave voluntarily; make sure it's not a 2-year lock).\n* **Start Date / Meta Vest Timing:** Pick a start date that allows you to collect any imminent Meta quarterly vest or bonus payout before giving notice, maximizing your overlap.\n* **Team & Scope Confirmation:** Reconfirm that you are landing on the specific team, scope, and Product Area (PA) you discussed during interviews.\n\n---\n\n### 4. How to Accept Gracefully\n\nSend a positive email to lock it in:\n\n> *\"Hi [Recruiter Name],*\n> \n> *Thank you for working with leadership to put this together. I really appreciate the team\u2019s effort to make the numbers work. I am thrilled to accept the offer and look forward to joining the team.*\n> \n> *Please send over the updated formal offer letter, and let's coordinate on start dates and next steps.\"*",
